    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Question\n\n![2025-01-08-140001_grim](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13e225b5-ccfd-411d-9ad3-b6814ae122d3)\r\n\r\nMini indentscope renders here. I have no idea why. I could disable it with this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n            local disableIndent = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].miniindentscope_disable = true end\r\n            vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('Filetype', { pattern = 'fzf', callback = disableIndent })\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs this a bug? Is there a better solution?",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.indentscope</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/402052/401153527-13e225b5-ccfd-411d-9ad3-b6814ae122d3.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMyNDgsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1Mjk0OCwicGF0aCI6Ii80MDIwNTIvNDAxMTUzNTI3LTEzZTIyNWI1LWNjZmQtNDExZC05YWQzLWI2ODE0YWUxMjJkMy5wbmc_.y_AP17zaYMgDMl5VaKNUcngbH_FTRASh-HbmKpPT16g\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/402052/401153527-13e225b5-ccfd-411d-9ad3-b6814ae122d3.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMyNDgsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1Mjk0OCwicGF0aCI6Ii80MDIwNTIvNDAxMTUzNTI3LTEzZTIyNWI1LWNjZmQtNDExZC05YWQzLWI2ODE0YWUxMjJkMy5wbmc_.y_AP17zaYMgDMl5VaKNUcngbH_FTRASh-HbmKpPT16g\" alt=\"2025-01-08-140001_grim\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mini indentscope renders here. I have no idea why. I could disable it with this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"            local disableIndent = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].miniindentscope_disable = true end\n            vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('Filetype', { pattern = 'fzf', callback = disableIndent })\n\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">            <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">disableIndent</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>) <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">miniindentscope_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n            <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>Filetype<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>fzf<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">disableIndent</span> })\n</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is this a bug? Is there a better solution?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.indentscope\nQuestion\n\nMini indentscope renders here. I have no idea why. I could disable it with this:\n            local disableIndent = function(args) vim.b[args.buf].miniindentscope_disable = true end\n            vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('Filetype', { pattern = 'fzf', callback = disableIndent })\n\nIs this a bug? Is there a better solution?",
