            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I can not reproduce this. Have you tried updating 'fzf-lua' to the *latest* `main`? There were attempts at implementing \"Normal-terminal\" which *might* trigger 'mini.indentscope' animation (as there are `ModeChanged` event triggers).\r\n\r\nDisabling it in 'fzf' filetype is a suggested solution here. The slightly better approach would be to just put `vim.b.miniindentscope_disable = true` inside '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/fzf.lua'.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I can not reproduce this. Have you tried updating 'fzf-lua' to the <em>latest</em> <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code>? There were attempts at implementing \"Normal-terminal\" which <em>might</em> trigger 'mini.indentscope' animation (as there are <code class=\"notranslate\">ModeChanged</code> event triggers).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Disabling it in 'fzf' filetype is a suggested solution here. The slightly better approach would be to just put <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.b.miniindentscope_disable = true</code> inside '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/fzf.lua'.</p>",
            "bodyText": "I can not reproduce this. Have you tried updating 'fzf-lua' to the latest main? There were attempts at implementing \"Normal-terminal\" which might trigger 'mini.indentscope' animation (as there are ModeChanged event triggers).\nDisabling it in 'fzf' filetype is a suggested solution here. The slightly better approach would be to just put vim.b.miniindentscope_disable = true inside '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/fzf.lua'.",
